From: Brian 'redbeard' Harrington <redbeard@dead-city.org>
Subject: [PATCH 12/12] Platform/Spacemit/K3: Cpu.asl _LPI first cut + \_SB platform _OSC (Task 9)

Platform/Spacemit/K3: Cpu.asl _LPI first cut + \_SB platform _OSC (Task 9)

Add _LPI to every ACPI0007 processor device: two non-retentive
platform states per the FFH spec and the HSM suspend audit
(task9-hsm-suspend-audit-2026-11-20.md):

- CPU_NR: FFH address (1<<60)|0x90000000, min-residency 950us,
  wake 500us
- CLUSTER_NR: FFH address (1<<60)|0x91000000, min-residency 2700us,
  wake 1100us

Both use the proven PMU vote + WFI + in-place-resume mechanism from
k3_corepm.c; the kernel's RISC-V LPI backend requires >1 flattened
state, so both are exposed. Package layout per ACPI 6.5 _LPI:
{MinResidency, WakeLatency, Count, StatePkgs...} (iASL-validated).
Latencies are the vendor DT values - measure before freezing.

Add the \\_SB platform-wide _OSC (UUID 0811B06E-...) confirming
PCLPI (0x80) ONLY: acpi_processor_get_lpi_info() gates _LPI parsing
on osc_pc_lpi_support_confirmed, which is set exclusively by this
handshake. Without it, _LPI is silently ignored (pr_debug-only
failure) - root cause of the first v13 boot showing _LPI in the
DSDT, processor devices bound, and no cpuidle. PR3/S3, GED,
hotplug-OST are not confirmed (no power resources / GPE wiring);
unknown UUIDs return _OSC failure.

Validation: full RELEASE build; built DSDT decodes 8x _LPI (both
states, correct FFH addresses) and the \\_SB _OSC with the PCLPI
mask. Hardware verification: the NEXT boot cycle (expect 'platform
_OSC: OS control mask' with 0x80, cpuidle LPI-0/1/2 states, usage
counts increasing, wake-source integrity per the v13 checklist).
---
